---
description: Use when deciding what a new or changed test should cover, or reviewing whether an existing test proves the right thing. Do not use for Playwright/Vitest configuration or CI wiring — see verification-git.mdc for that.
globs:
  - "test/**/*"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Test observable behaviour through the public seam — rendered output, a
  composable's returned value, a route's response — not an internal
  implementation detail. A test that mirrors internals breaks on every
  refactor and proves nothing about correctness.
- Pick the smallest seam that proves the change: prefer a fast Vitest unit
  test over a Playwright E2E test whenever a unit test can prove the same
  thing. Reserve E2E for a real user-facing path (rendering, navigation,
  interaction) that a unit test cannot observe.
- Mock or stub only at a real I/O or time boundary (a fetch call, a server
  integration); never mock the unit under test itself.
- Give each test one assertion cluster and a name in the form
  `condition → expected outcome`, not a vague "works" description.
- A good test is fast, isolated, repeatable, and self-validating. A flaky or
  order-dependent test is a liability, not coverage — fix or remove it rather
  than retrying past it.
